        An adjunction core extends to an adjuction iff <fr:tex>∀a,b ∈ A. ∀x ∈ X.</fr:tex>
        <fr:link
href="subb-000E.xml"
type="local"
addr="subb-000E">I</fr:link> commutes, and iff <fr:tex>∀x,y ∈ X. a ∈ A.</fr:tex> <fr:link
href="subbb-000E.xml"
type="local"
addr="subbb-000E">II</fr:link>
        commutes.
        The adjunction is unique when it exists.
    </fr:p><fr:p>
        The <fr:link
href="street-2012.xml"
type="local"
addr="street-2012">original theorem</fr:link> is stated in terms of
        <fr:tex>\mathcal {V}</fr:tex>-enriched categories, but we only treat the simple case
        of Homset-categories here.
